    {
      "id": "S-BERNOULLI-APP",
      "kind": "BACKGROUND_PREREQUISITE",
      "formula": "For C2compact, entropy of real-product sum law <=half sum of shifted squared integrals",
      "classification": "EXTERNAL_HEADER_CUT",
      "anchors": [
        {
          "input_role": "external_Bernoulli_app",
          "start_line": 1600,
          "end_line": 1613,
          "literal_LF_sha256": "960f0a9846d2bf4aff0a0c629cc333e8b2e65b3cf9a8d12286ab2ce3e8051c29",
          "literal": "For f ∈ C_c²(ℝ) (compactly supported, twice continuously differentiable), the entropy\nof f² under the law of the Rademacher sum S_{n+1} is bounded by half the expected\nsum of squared differences:\n\n  Ent_{S_{n+1}}(f²) ≤ (1/2) · ∑ᵢ E[(f(S_{n+1}) - f(S_{n+1} with coord i flipped))²]\n\nThis is the continuous-function version of the Bernoulli log-Sobolev inequality,\nwhich serves as a key intermediate step toward the Gaussian log-Sobolev inequality\nvia the central limit theorem. -/\ntheorem bernoulli_logSobolev_app {f : ℝ → ℝ} (hf : CompactlySupportedSmooth f) (n : ℕ) :\n    LogSobolev.entropy (rademacherLaw (n + 1)).toMeasure (fun x => (f x)^2) ≤\n    (1/2) * ∑ i : Fin (n + 1), ∫ x,\n        (f (rademacherSumProd (n + 1) x) - f (rademacherSumShifted (n + 1) i x))^2\n          ∂rademacherProductMeasure (n + 1) := by\n"
        }
      ],
      "proof_boundary": "Transfer/Bernoulli assembly1614-1634 excluded; actual34 count theorem is genuine local alternative."
    },
    {
      "id": "S-LHS",
      "kind": "SOURCE_PROOF_NODE",
      "formula": "h_lhs: successor source entropy tends toGaussian entropy by tendsto_entropy_f_sq hf",
      "classification": "EXTERNAL_SOURCE",
